WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.780
Over two thousand years ago, the Greek
philosopher Epicurus is credited with a

2
00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.020
few short questions.

3
00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:10.640
Is God willing to prevent
evil, but not able?

4
00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.240
Is God able, but not willing?

5
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:17.850
The questions grow sharper when the one
suffering is a child caught in a war,

6
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.900
or an animal in a fire.

7
00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:25.130
If God is all-powerful and
all-loving, why do children suffer?

8
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.680
In this mission, you'll sort
moral evil from natural evil,

9
00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:32.110
and read those questions as
David Hume recorded them.

10
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.670
Then you'll ask what innocent suffering
means for trust in God's care,

11
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.900
and weigh up whether
suffering disproves God.

12
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:45.090
Your mission: explain why suffering
raises such a hard question about God.
